{"c":[{"id":"0df170c8a6eff7e0","sum":"OWNER_NOTE_CHARS is 0 behind TODO(INT1); privacy copy is bundled PrivacyPromise.txt (verify gate). Scope stand-ins use builders.scopeLabel. Script env names via processEnv/HELPER_ONLY_ENV. Diff adversary accept runs vs base before loosening a guard.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"661702e6fd19a6cd","sum":"OWNER_NOTE_CHARS is 0 behind TODO(INT1); onboarding promise is bundle PrivacyPromise.txt (CARET_VERIFY_PRIVACY_RESOURCE gate); canned oracle once flaked on the 15 ms generator budget, so rerun before calling a drop; scope stand-ins read labels via builders.ts scopeLabel.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e3e2ae3d8390c6b7","sum":"OWNER_NOTE_CHARS is 0 behind TODO(INT1) (grep it to restore 2,000). Onboarding's privacyLine reads bundled PrivacyPromise.txt (nil under swift run/xctest; tests inject one); CARET_VERIFY_PRIVACY_RESOURCE refuses an app whose copy is missing or differs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T030901Z-f494e5b78b4262d5","text":"INT1 (v2/int1): OWNER_NOTE_CHARS is 0 behind TODO(INT1) until HA2's allotment is re-expressed on the output-based ledger; the tests that need it are skipped or floored with TODO(INT1). grep TODO(INT1) to restore 2,000.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T053436Z-ced2cc8130be00ef","text":"Onboarding promise: PermissionsScreen.privacyLine reads bundle PrivacyPromise.txt (nil under swift run/xctest); renders and tests inject their own PrivacyPromise. CARET_VERIFY_PRIVACY_RESOURCE: gate refuses a finished app whose copy is missing, empty or not PRIVACY_PROMISE.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3a15d551c65db7c1","sum":"Elapsed-time candidate cuts made the canned Ask oracle load-sensitive. Scope-ask stand-ins use builders.scopeLabel, never wording regexes. An askAnswer with no picks is valid only beside a question's filling labels.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T080402Z-28411e2e4fbdeba1","text":"realfill-asks canned oracle: fill's 15 ms wall-clock candidate budget (GENERATOR_BUDGET_MS) flips a single run's Ask right->refused about 1 in 20 under load; rerun or loop one Ask before calling an oracle drop a regression (G35 b31-04, ask-17).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T080402Z-5b6ab755f2bbf6d7","text":"Scope-ask stand-ins read the field label with test/builders.ts scopeLabel (wording: Field: \"<label>\". Control: ...); never regex the wording in a test. An askAnswer with no picks is valid only beside a question's filling labels.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"90e1c122d2365aa7","sum":"Script env names go through processEnv()/HELPER_ONLY_ENV; tests await PageFocus.moved. Diff guard-adversary accept attempts vs base before loosening a guard. Value questions need a consumer declaring askValues; realfill-asks scores AskAsks.fallback as automatic.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"efc720c8ec4faf9a","sum":"Scripts read env names through processEnv() and HELPER_ONLY_ENV (host-env.test.ts scans only helper/src), so new script env names go there; tests await PageFocus.moved for walk/focus completion, since EngineSession.onFocus discards it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T094208Z-4d056099840ba76b","text":"host-env.test.ts scans only helper/src for process.env; helper/scripts/privacy-gate.ts still reads its build-gate names (CARET_INTERNAL_BUILD, CARET_*PRIVACY_RESOURCE) through processEnv() and HELPER_ONLY_ENV, so new script env names go there too.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T100347Z-137d3d2067c38ff7","text":"Tests can await PageFocus.moved for the walk/focus completion; EngineSession.onFocus discards that promise.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"49be5dc02d9c236a","sum":"Before loosening a fill guard, diff guard-adversary accept attempts vs base (oneOfSeveral also blocks role-labelled people's phones). Value questions reach only consumers declaring askValues; realfill-asks scores AskAsks.fallback as automatic, picks as after-pick.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T103008Z-ae509cb3a9a659fb","text":"G36: before loosening a fill guard, diff guard-adversary --verifier accept attempts vs base; oneOfSeveral also blocks role-labelled people's phones (recruiter: Wren Ng, ...). page-w3 1f flaked once in the full fast suite, passes alone.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T103634Z-919e960bf3dcead3","text":"VS1: value questions reach only consumers whose hello declares askValues beside askChoices; realfill-asks scores a value question's AskAsks.fallback as the automatic result and its scripted picks as 'after pick'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8a060c9a1acff6b1","sum":"Info.plist double-hyphen comment refuses builds; h1x build.sh hardcodes worktree; cp -cR breaks symlinked node_modules. Disclosure caps at 8 ways (rebuilds need 'plan'); value options state exact outputs. Helper stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS; realfill-asks seals requests first.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cd83d1662f3b8183","sum":"HI2: Info.plist comment with a double hyphen refuses every build; h1x harness build.sh hardcodes its worktree, cp -cR breaks symlinked node_modules. VS1: Disclosure caps at 8 ways (rebuilt requests need 'plan'); value options state exact outputs (builders.ts optionIs).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c6064da85f9f18d6","sum":"Build gotchas (HI2): a double hyphen in an Info.plist XML comment refuses every build-app.sh mode (the gate parses it); h11/h13/h14 harness build.sh exports from a hardcoded worktree on v2/host and cp -cR turns a symlinked node_modules into a dangling link.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T080815Z-40413337304fea62","text":"The privacy gate parses apps/caret/Bundle/Info.plist as XML, so a double hyphen inside an XML comment refuses every build-app.sh mode (v2/onboard-privacy ccff2558 rewords it; HI2).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T080815Z-5040e69897a0bba9","text":"VM harness build.sh (h11/h13/h14) exports from a hardcoded worktree W, requires the commit on v2/host, and clones W's node_modules with cp -cR, which copies a symlinked node_modules as a dangling link (HI2).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"84a4af324deddcaf","sum":"VS1: Disclosure composes at most 8 ways, so a request rebuilt after the verifier minted its parts as plan text needs 'plan' in its shape slot. Ask value options read 'Proposed value: \"…\". Source: …'; stand-ins match them with builders.ts optionIs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T103634Z-c66a1e426ad50081","text":"VS1: Disclosure composes at most MAX_WAYS (8) ways; past that a text carries every reason of its parts, so a request rebuilt after the verifier minted its parts as plan text needs 'plan' in its shape slot.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T103634Z-ffaa923aad520f1c","text":"VS1: an Ask's value options state exact outputs ('Proposed value: \"…\". Source: …'); test stand-ins match them with test/builders.ts optionIs, while a fill on focus keeps its quoted-candidate criteria.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ad5eb36f5863fc8a","sum":"Helper tests: generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not time; close page sessions before Helper.shutdown. Oracle: realfill-asks seals requests first, so keep oracle rules off FillTrace. Unit-based choices only for Asks naming the source window.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"78a720eef0312ba1","sum":"Helper tests: candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not time (stats.ms is diagnostic; a cap stop marks a partial window cut); close page sessions before Helper.shutdown and Store.close, or a trailing walk hits a closed store.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T122806Z-20adf579b39b18f9","text":"Candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not elapsed time; no setGeneratorClock, budgetMs or --generator-clock override remains. stats.ms is diagnostic, and a visit-cap stop still marks a partial window cut.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T131449Z-7a0add213d3fc6e0","text":"Tests that wire page sessions into Helper must close those sessions before Helper.shutdown and Store.close; a scheduled trailing walk otherwise reaches a closed store.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"71e3e7853f09b491","sum":"Oracle and choices: realfill-asks seals requests before the canned oracle answers, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there; keep oracle rules off the trace. A source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent, so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T143933Z-2d2e0e57729d25b3","text":"realfill-asks seals each request before the canned oracle answers it, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there: the oracle reads fill questions by their text on the scoreboard but by the trace in the vs1 kit (runB31). Don't make oracle rules depend on the trace.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T143933Z-70fb13e0b1aaff9c","text":"v2/choices: a source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent; a TextEdit note never fits an Ask that does not name it (prose share keeps half back), so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices. The user's request is always a basis.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
